============================================================
WWLAN-3626: SoftAP 5G/6G throughput degradation
============================================================

ISSUE

6 GHz TCP throughput was around 429 Mbps against a 720 Mbps criterion. UDP showed 48-55% packet loss. This was a regression from Beta RC2 to RC3.

WORKAROUND

1. Checked RSSI, MCS and channel bandwidth.
2. Checked channel utilization.
3. Compared TCP and UDP behavior.
4. Compared RC3 with the previous working RC2 build.
5. High UDP packet loss pointed towards a packet delivery issue rather than only a TCP problem.
6. Narrowed the issue towards the FW TX scheduler.
7. Provided the throughput and packet-loss data to the FW team.

RESOLUTION

FW scheduler issue was fixed. Fix was validated and the throughput/traffic behavior was retested.


============================================================
W5312-6334: SoftAP creation failure in MCU mode
============================================================

ISSUE

SoftAP creation was failing on SYN5312 MCU mode and the issue was blocking the Beta release. There was no wl tool or dmesg, so UART logs were used.

WORKAROUND

1. Captured the UART console during SoftAP creation.
2. Checked the FW error message from the UART log.
3. Compared the 5312 SoftAP bring-up sequence with the working 4384 sequence.
4. Found the difference in the initialization sequence.
5. Shared the step-by-step comparison with the FW team.

RESOLUTION

FW team identified a missing initialization step in the MCU-mode AP bring-up and fixed it through an emergency patch. Beta release proceeded.


============================================================
WWLAN-3563: Kernel RSN capability regression
============================================================

ISSUE

After upgrading the Linux kernel from 6.2 to 6.11, the DUT failed to associate with certain APs. The same FW worked with kernel 6.2.

WORKAROUND

1. Captured the Association Request using a sniffer.
2. Checked the RSN IE.
3. Found RSN Capabilities as 0x008c instead of 0x0080.
4. Tested the same FW with kernel 6.2 and 6.11.
5. 6.2 worked and 6.11 failed.
6. This isolated the issue to the kernel/cfg80211 side.

RESOLUTION

Kernel team identified the cfg80211 RSN IE construction change and provided a patch. Association was restored after the patch.


