W5312-4781: SoftAP first-ping delay
============================================================

ISSUE

After a client associated to the SYN5312 SoftAP, the first ping took more than 5 seconds. On the 4384 Linux-hosted platform the ping was immediate.

WORKAROUND

1. Reproduced the delay after SoftAP client association.
2. Compared the same flow on the 4384 platform.
3. Checked the DHCP startup behavior.
4. Found that the MCU-mode DHCP server was starting slowly.
5. Compared the different platform bring-up behavior.

RESOLUTION

RCA was the slow DHCP server startup in MCU mode. The issue was identified as a platform-specific startup behavior.


============================================================
W43756-534 / W43756-576: NAT Keep-Alive version mismatch
============================================================

ISSUE

NAT Keep-Alive worked on 43756E PCIe but returned a version mismatch on SDIO using the same chip/FW.

WORKAROUND

1. Ran the same `wl mkeep_alive` command on PCIe and SDIO.
2. PCIe returned version 1 successfully.
3. SDIO returned version mismatch.
4. Compared the DHD driver path between PCIe and SDIO.
5. Isolated the mismatch to the SDIO DHD branch expecting a different version format.

RESOLUTION

The issue was isolated to the SDIO DHD driver path rather than the FW. The driver/FW version-format mismatch was identified for correction.
